    "instructions": "Heat the oven to 375°F and grease a 9x13-inch baking dish.\nMelt half the butter with half the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the mushrooms and onion with salt and pepper for 5 minutes, then stir in the garlic for 20 seconds.\nSpread half the mushroom mixture in the baking dish and keep the rest aside.\nSeason the chicken with salt, pepper, garlic powder, paprika and Italian seasoning. Brown it in the rest of the butter and oil, about 2 minutes per side, and lay it over the mushrooms.\nPour the broth into the skillet, scrape up the browned bits and boil 4-5 minutes to reduce.\nCover the chicken with the remaining mushrooms, then the mozzarella, and pour the reduced broth over.\nBake uncovered about 15 minutes, until the chicken is cooked through. Garnish with parsley.",
