      {
        "name": "green onion",
        "quantity": 2,
        "unit": "tablespoon",
        "notes": "sliced, 2-3 tablespoons"
      }
    ],
    "instructions": "Heat the oven to 350°F and grease a 9x13-inch baking dish.\nMix the chicken with 1 cup of the cheese, fill each tortilla, roll up and set seam side down in the dish.\nMelt the butter in a skillet, whisk in the flour and cook 1 minute.\nOff the heat, whisk in the broth, then return to the heat and cook until thickened and bubbly.\nLet the sauce cool 3-5 minutes so the sour cream won't curdle, then stir in the sour cream and green chilies until smooth.\nPour the sauce over the enchiladas and top with the remaining cheese.\nBake 20-25 minutes until bubbly and heated through, then broil briefly until the top is golden.\nTop with sliced green onions and serve.",
