    ],
    "instructions": "Heat the oven to 375°F.\nSeparate the dough into 8 triangles and pat each out slightly.\nLay 3 slightly overlapping pepperoni slices in the center of each triangle.\nSprinkle about 1 tablespoon of mozzarella on each.\nRoll each triangle up from the short side toward the opposite point and set point side down on an ungreased baking sheet.\nBake 12-15 minutes until golden brown.\nServe warm with heated marinara or pizza sauce for dipping.",
