    "instructions": "Heat the oven to 350°F and line a baking sheet with parchment.\nMix 1/2 cup of the marinara with the panko, Parmesan, onion, parsley, seasonings, egg, balsamic and Worcestershire, then gently work in the turkey by hand.\nShape into an 8x4-inch loaf on the sheet and spread the remaining 1/2 cup marinara on top.\nBake on the middle rack 45-50 minutes until a thermometer reads 160°F. Add extra Parmesan in the last 10 minutes if you like, then rest 10 minutes before slicing.\nMeanwhile, cover the potatoes with salted water, bring to a boil, then simmer 15-18 minutes until fork-tender.\nRaise the oven to 400°F, line a sheet with parchment and drain the potatoes onto it.\nSmash each potato to about 1/2 inch thick, drizzle with olive oil, season with salt, pepper and rosemary.\nBake about 20 minutes, sprinkle with Parmesan and bake 2-3 minutes more until melted. Serve hot.",
