    "instructions": "Bring a big pot of well-salted water to a boil, cook the noodles al dente while the sauce comes together, and drain.\nMelt 2 tablespoons of the butter in a large sauté pan over medium-high heat. Season the steak with salt and pepper and sear it in a single layer for about 3 minutes, then flip and brown 2-3 minutes more. Work in batches if needed and set the steak aside.\nMelt the remaining butter in the pan and cook the onion for 3 minutes. Add the mushrooms and cook 5-7 minutes until soft, then the garlic for 1 minute.\nPour in the wine, scrape up the browned bits and let it reduce for 3 minutes.\nWhisk the stock, Worcestershire and flour until smooth, add to the pan and simmer 5 minutes, stirring now and then.\nStir in the yogurt and the steak, season to taste, and serve over the noodles with parsley.",
